{"author":{"id":"dec876858d28babbadcead4137861bf586626b8518cbce9c5f4fc52ac3b424b8"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1792709499,"nonce":"nwOeKIPG/z3yBwsIGA/v03ZIC70=","message":"Implementation and scoped evidence\n\nCollectedTextPath now retains the LayoutNodeId of its owning 3D layer, if any. Layer preparation keeps each run's own auxiliary rows, offsets its scissor into the local viewport and conjugates collected CSS glyph affines into that viewport. The 3D bake accumulates TextBatch rather than bare glyphs, rebases references and restores matching rows/atlases for direct and converted text.\n\nAn inside contour keeps its captured frame with the layer origin subtracted. An outside ancestor contour is pulled back from screen space onto the layer plane with the inverse of the existing Y-then-X perspective map before rasterization. Its projection therefore remains stationary on screen. Invalid, singular or behind-camera vertex mappings produce an empty clip. No shader, GPU layout, shared ClipPath/CSS fill-rule or layout promotion changes.\n\nPre-wiring public control failed at (95,24), [22,0,181,255] expected blue, with compositor=false, inside=true, angle=0, DPI=1, Path, full paint. /private/tmp/blinc-layer-text-negative.log. The initial public owner control passed after wiring. Expanded controls had one test-only diagnostic format-string compile error, corrected before execution; no production workaround.\n\nFour GPU controls and one CPU frame/projection control pass with normal storage and forced data-texture rendering. Coverage: public motion and surface-compositor entry, full/cache-eligible frames, Path/Polygon, inside and outside clip owners, nonzero origins, tilt 0/35/-25 degrees, DPI 1/1.5, shear/reflection and independent descendant translation, changed/empty/non-finite/removed contours, mixed direct/converted runs with different local clip owners, poisoned auxiliary upload and growth, and overlapping plain/affine paint order. The pixel controls use independent analytic triangle membership against an unclipped baseline, skip contour edges, and require ink both inside and outside. CPU controls cover composed X/Y projection and inverse round trips, reflection, fractional origins, native contour rows, immutable source frames, NaN and singular mappings.\n\nThe directly affected existing overlay public Path/Polygon GPU control and owned-payload clone/rebase CPU control also pass in both modes. Commands select blinc_app --lib with layer_text_clip or the exact overlay filters, with ignored GPU controls enabled and test-threads=1. CARGO_BUILD_JOBS=2, fallback primitive/glyph capacities 1024. Normal GPU controls were not repeated after CPU-only coverage was expanded. No workspace, DSL, docs, platform or unrelated gates. Touched-file rustfmt and diff checks pass. Temporary renderer capability flags restored.\n\nLogs: /private/tmp/blinc-layer-text-{normal,dt}-{cpu,app,overlay,ownership}.log where selected, plus negative/wiring/controls logs. Browser/mobile pixels and performance remain unverified. No new offscreen layer is added; existing per-layer textures are reused. Contour preparation, outside-vertex inverse mapping and row uploads are unbenchmarked.\n\nThis completes the remaining collected-text ownership path tracked by parent 732c3370857424d2e3c7ccfcde44fe0095471eda74dae4e5b415daca036738fe. It does not redesign nested 3D composition, existing rectangular ancestor scissor semantics, decoration/shadow rendering, other clip shapes, arbitrary stacked intersections or cross-stream isolation on e0a7502. CSS text promotion remains guarded off; no promoted-text live remapping is claimed. Nothing pushed.\n\nReview follow-up: the shared TextBatch renderer draws converted primitives before plain glyphs. A new overlapping 3D text control exposed reversed paint order, [247,8,0,255] at (27,22) where the green reference was [0,239,8,255]. The bake now coalesces consecutive runs using the same pipeline and starts a new owned batch at plain/affine boundaries, then replays those runs in collected order. No all-glyph conversion or glyph layout expansion is introduced. This can add draw calls at pipeline boundaries; it is unbenchmarked. All five 3D controls pass on the final source in storage and DT. The overlay controls were already complete with unchanged shared preparation code. Logs: /private/tmp/blinc-layer-text-order-{negative,fixed}.log and /private/tmp/blinc-layer-text-dt-ordered.log.","files":null}]}